  "review": {
    "objective": "#13",
    "delegation": "Kirk, 2026-11-16 (\"Rw13. Yes approve\"): an agent may approve this world's golden captures at their exact digests, after inspecting each one at its declared viewport and backend, and may record the composition review.",
    "reviewer": "Claude agent (Clockgrove owner session)",
    "scope": "All 78 CI captures from runs 43881218079 (main 3147efc) and 43885457259 (main 3d1ceec, which changes only .github/workflows/factory.yml), on Clockgrove 1e4b8b9. The two runs agree on every digest. 13 states x 3 viewports x WebGPU/WebGL2.",
    "findings": "Every file was inspected at its viewport and backend. Every file renders cleanly: no blank frames, missing textures or broken geometry. Text is legible, the rail, inspector, recovery and text-access content matches each state, and the quality tiers are ordered (the low tier draws no rain streaks by design). Each WebGL2 file differs from its WebGPU twin by 0 to 194 pixels, all inside the canvas. The magenta boxes in event-why-inspector are the intended wall-clock masks. The departures from the reference are in tests/visual/README.md, Composition review: the 17:45 dusk states lit like noon, the selection ring over the entity, the phone Why panel cut off, the layout and the raw ids. None of them is a rendering fault."
  }
